Fix PPZJ parton shower bug caused by MSTP(125)=2

MSTP(125)=2 preserves ISR shower history in the PYTHIA 6 event record.
This is required for the PPJJ process's special ISR handling (lines 1144-1370)
but breaks PPZJ/PPZQ/PPZG/PPWJ because:

  1. The jet parton gets an intermediate copy (K=13) instead of a direct
     final-state child (K=1)
  2. The LME finder locates this intermediate copy but cannot activate it
     (K=13 >= 11 fails the activation check)
  3. The actual final-state jet parton is never identified as the LME
  4. No partons enter MAKECASCADE: NSPLIT=0, NSCAT=0

Additionally, the DO 183 loop in 2.4.0 activates beam remnant baryons with
off-shell mass, causing ~7% spurious event discards. The simpler 2.2.0 logic
(deactivate all non-LME particles) avoids this.

Verification (1000 events, pp vacuum 8160 GeV, PTMIN=0, WEXPO=1.4):
  Before fix:  splittings=0.0   scatterings=0.0  discarded=55 (~5.5%)
  After fix:   splittings=2.27  scatterings=0.0  discarded=0

Verification (1000 events, pPb 8160 GeV with Trajectum 2D hydro, bin .10):
  Before fix:  splittings=0.0   scatterings=0.0  discarded=337 (~6.7%)
  After fix:   splittings=2.55  scatterings=19.1 discarded=0

--- jewel-2.4.0-2D/jewel-2.4.0.f
+++ jewel-2.4.0-2D-MOD/jewel-2.4.0.f
@@ -861,8 +861,8 @@

 C--initialise PYTHIA
-C--keep parton shower history in PYJETS
-	 MSTP(125)=2
+C--keep parton shower history in PYJETS (only needed for PPJJ ISR jeweling)
+	 IF(COLLIDER.EQ.'PPJJ') MSTP(125)=2
 C--no multiple interactions
 	 MSTP(81) = 0
@@ -1461,17 +1461,25 @@
 	  PID=K(LME1,2)
 	  ENI=MAX(P(LME1,4),P(LME2,4))
+	  if (collider.eq.'PPJJ') then
 	  DO 183 IPART=OFFSET+1, OFFSET+NPART
 	   IF((IPART.NE.LME1).AND.(IPART.NE.LME2)
      &		.AND.(K(IPART,1).LT.11)) then
 	     if (p(ipart,5).gt.pymass(k(ipart,2))) then
 	       k(ipart,1)=1
 	     else
-     	       if ((isparton(k(ipart,2))).and.
+              if ((isparton(k(ipart,2))).and.
      &		(abs(pyp(ipart,19)).lt.etamax)) then
 		    if (p(ipart,5).gt.0.d0) call makemassless(ipart,lme1,lme2)
 		    k(ipart,1)=1
-		 else
+		 else
 		    k(ipart,1)=4
-		 endif
+		 endif
            endif
-         endif
+         endif
 	   if (k(ipart,2).eq.22) k(ipart,1)=4
- 183    CONTINUE
+ 183    CONTINUE
+	  else
+	  DO 283 IPART=OFFSET+1, OFFSET+NPART
+	   IF((IPART.NE.LME1).AND.(IPART.NE.LME2)
+     &      .AND.(K(IPART,1).LT.11))
+     &      K(IPART,1)=4
+	   if (k(ipart,2).eq.22) k(ipart,1)=4
+ 283    CONTINUE
+	  endif
